02 The French Revolution and its reach
Unequal privilege and state debt ; then Tax reform fails and the Estates-General meets ; then Dispute over representation becomes a sovereignty struggle ; then Mass action breaks old institutions and radicalises reform ;
then Rights spread, alongside violence and authoritarian reaction

06 Nationalism and the making of Europe
Revolutionary citizenship challenges dynastic loyalty ; then Print, schooling and markets widen shared identities ;
then Liberal movements demand constitutions and national unity ; then Statesmen use diplomacy and war to reshape territories ; then National unity can turn into exclusion and great-power rivalry

08 Japan's path to industrial power
Western pressure exposes vulnerability ; then Meiji leaders centralise political and fiscal authority ; then Education, military and infrastructure reforms build capacity ; then Imported technology and state support accelerate industry ;
then Industrial strength supports both sovereignty and expansion

09 China: empire, revolution and state-building
Foreign pressure and domestic crisis weaken Qing rule ; then Limited reforms fail to settle legitimacy and power ;
then The 1911 Revolution ends the dynasty but leaves fragmentation ; then Nationalists and communists compete through war and mobilisation ; then The 1949 revolution combines unification with a new social project

16 Decolonisation as a process
Colonial extraction and exclusion create organised opposition ; then War weakens imperial resources and prestige ;
then Mass mobilisation raises the costs of colonial rule ; then Negotiation, revolution or armed struggle transfers power ; then New states confront nation-building and economic dependence

18 Malaya and Southeast Asian decolonisation
Colonial economic and ethnic divisions shape unequal interests ; then Japanese occupation disrupts the old order ;
then Post-war constitutional plans and insurgency create conflict ; then Security policy overlaps with inter-community bargaining ; then Independence arrives before every political and security problem ends
